# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git normalises text to LF in the repository and checks it out as CRLF on
# Windows, which is fine for almost everything here. The exceptions are the
# files that get executed by Linux: a shell script or a Dockerfile carrying
# CRLF fails inside a container with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M",
# which is an unhelpful way to spend an evening. Those are pinned to LF
# everywhere, including in the Windows working copy.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Binary — never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text. Parquet in
# particular would be corrupted by any normalisation.
*.parquet   binary
*.duckdb    binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.xls       binary
*.xlsm      binary
*.zip       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
